Subject: [PATCH] compositor: destroy the clients before clearing the windows on exit

For Hyprland v0.55.2 (39d7e20). Optional: use it on top of
hyprland-exit-crash.patch (the layout guards) or on its own. Applies on top
of astroland's hyprland_clamp_to_border.patch too.

This is the root cause of the crash on exit with tiled windows open.
CCompositor::cleanup() clears m_workspaces and m_windows first, and only
then destroys the clients (wl_display_destroy_clients()), when the monitors
are gone too. After m_windows.clear(), a window's last strong reference is
the render pass of the last frame (each CSurfacePassElement holds a
PHLWINDOW). When the first client is destroyed, its window unmaps and makes
a snapshot. The snapshot's beginRender() clears the render pass, so the
other windows are freed on the spot, without unmapWindow().
~CWindow() doesn't take a window's target out of its layout, so dwindle and
master keep nodes with expired targets and crash in calculateWorkspace()
when the unmapping window's removeTarget() recalculates. Windows the last
frame didn't draw are freed by m_windows.clear() itself, the same way.

This destroys the clients first, while the windows, workspaces and monitors
still exist (the plugins are already unloaded). Every window then leaves its
layout through the same unmap/destroy path as when a client disconnects at
runtime. XWayland still goes first, as before, so its X11 windows get their
destroy (~CXWM emits it for every surface) while they still exist too.
Clearing m_windows after that frees windows that are no longer in any
layout.

The old order dates from when m_windows held unique pointers. db91d949
("compositor: move wl_display_destroy_clients", 2024-04) moved the call
above g_pInputManager.reset() for the same kind of reason: destroying
clients reaches managers that must still exist. Since windows became shared
pointers (bca7804b, 2024-04-27), references other than m_windows can keep
them alive past m_windows.clear().

diff --git a/src/Compositor.cpp b/src/Compositor.cpp
index d2fe2f9..087452f 100644
--- a/src/Compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/Compositor.cpp
@@ -565,6 +565,14 @@ void CCompositor::cleanup() {
     // still in a normal working state.
     g_pPluginSystem->unloadAllPlugins();
 
+    // destroy the clients while the windows, workspaces and monitors still exist, so that every
+    // window leaves its layout the normal way (unmap / destroy). With m_windows cleared first, a
+    // window's last reference is the last frame's render pass, which the first unmap's snapshot
+    // clears: the other windows are then freed without an unmap, and their layout nodes expire.
+    g_pXWayland.reset();
+
+    wl_display_destroy_clients(g_pCompositor->m_wlDisplay);
+
     m_workspaces.clear();
     m_windows.clear();
 
@@ -572,11 +580,8 @@ void CCompositor::cleanup() {
         g_pHyprOpenGL->destroyMonitorResources(m);
     }
 
-    g_pXWayland.reset();
-
     m_monitors.clear();
 
-    wl_display_destroy_clients(g_pCompositor->m_wlDisplay);
     removeAllSignals();
 
     g_pInputManager.reset();
